    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="427c754c-37df-5878-9e9b-942b4c7d1d1b" activityNameId="6d73bc7c-427e-59ab-ae86-2a98870bef9a" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Solar system, 12 m2 Cu flat plate collector, one-family house, combined system</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Solar system, 12 m2 Cu flat plate collector, one-family house, combined system
Solar system with a flat plate collector on a one family house with a combined system for hot water and heating. 25 years life time,  35 m pipe length and 1100 l heat storage. ;
Synonyms: SFD, one-family house; 
UUID: 95ecd53e-cc69-3878-9336-cf25555d4d15
Production and disposal of a complete solar system (excluding auxiliary heating). Including different components, heat exchange fluid, warm water pipes, transports of parts to CH, and delivery with a van.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Solar collector system for room heating and hot water installed on the roof of a house.
Time period: Time of simulation.
Production volume: 10'433 systems with flat plate collectors were sold in 2008. 29.3% of the area is installed on one-family houses for heating and hot water.
Sampling: Own simulation. 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_95ecd53e-cc69-3878-9336-cf25555d4d15.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
